---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What this static Conflict Protocol site does and does not collect."
  canonical="/privacy/"
>
  <article class="article-shell">
    <header class="content-hero">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
        <h1>Short version: this site is quiet.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Conflict Protocol is a static V1 site. No accounts, no forms, no comments, no newsletter box
          waiting in the bushes.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="article-body">
      <h2>What the site collects</h2>
      <p>
        The site itself does not collect personal data. There are no user accounts, sign-ins, contact
        forms, comments, purchases, or email capture in V1.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        There is no analytics script in V1. No Google Analytics, no pixels, no heatmaps, no session
        replay. If analytics gets added later, this page needs to change before that ships.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The planned host is Cloudflare Pages. Like any web host, Cloudflare may process basic request
        information needed to serve the site, such as IP address, browser details, request URL, and
        timestamps. That is hosting infrastructure, not a Conflict Protocol account system.
      </p>

      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        Some links may take you to the game or to safety resources. Those sites have their own privacy
        practices. Once you leave this site, their rules apply.
      </p>

      <h2>If this changes</h2>
      <p>
        If the site adds forms, accounts, analytics, email capture, or anything else that collects data,
        this page should say that plainly. No fog machine, no fake legal opera.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
